## Layout

| Path | Role |
|---|---|
| `manifest.yaml` | The manifest — the 1.0.0 contract, declared before any script runs |
| `inputs/SOURCES.md` | Where every input comes from, and under what licence |
| `scripts/` | The code that turns inputs into outputs |
| `outputs/` | The raw measurements produced by the scripts |
| `analysis/metrics.json` | The machine-readable metrics extracted from outputs |
| `analysis/ANALYSIS.md` | The prose reading of those metrics |
| `figures/FIGURES.md` | The figures index — one entry per rendered figure |
{%- if type == 'hypothesis_testing' %}
| `freeze/model_spec.json` | The pre-registered specification, frozen before measuring |
{%- endif %}

{% if type == 'hypothesis_testing' -%}
## Pre-registration

`freeze/model_spec.json` is filled and **committed before** the first
measurement. It stays versioned on purpose: a downstream check proves
antecedence by git genealogy, so a git-ignored freeze would destroy the proof.
{%- else -%}
## No freeze

A `{{ type }}` experiment states no falsifiable hypothesis, so it
carries no `freeze/` directory. Switch the kind to `hypothesis_testing` when a
prediction has to be pre-registered before measuring.
{%- endif %}

## Validation split

This package (axm-init) owns the *rendered* surface: the tree, the manifest
keys, their choice sets and the git-ignore policy. The *semantic* contract of
the manifest — its model, its cross-field rules — lives in axm-lab and is
validated there. Neither side imports the other.
